WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.380
Now that we have covered the legal protections in place, let's look at what this looks like

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.920
in the real world.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.740
On the screen is a video titled Life and Death Drama.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:15.460
As we watch this, I want you to notice that sudden cardiac arrest can truly happen to

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:21.780
anyone, regardless of their age, race, gender, or demographic.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:26.820
Even though there are often stereotypes about who is at risk, these examples show that cardiac

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:31.959
arrest does not discriminate and can happen to anyone at any time.

00:00:31.959 --> 00:00:36.880
I want you to notice a specific detail in how these individuals fall.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.279
Notice that they do not put out their hands to brace themselves.

00:00:40.279 --> 00:00:45.520
This is because cardiac arrest causes the heart to stop pumping blood immediately.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.880
Because blood flow to the brain is cut off instantly, the person loses consciousness

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.919
and collapses without any warning or time to react.

00:00:53.919 --> 00:00:59.560
Recognizing this sudden unprotected collapse is a key way for you to identify that someone

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:00.880
needs your help right away.

